jobs_results.description:
SD Worx is a leading European provider of Payroll & HR services with global reach. We have offices in Europe and an office in Mauritius. Our goal? We bring people solutions to life. So, companies of any size can turn Human Resources into a source of value for the business and the people in it. Our people solutions span the entire employee journey, from getting people paid to attracting, rewarding, and developing talent. Are you ready to join us?

Global Services provides payroll and HR solutions for international organizations active in multiple countries with more than 100 employees. Global Services is part of SD Worx and SD Worx is the foremost market leader in this segment of the market, thanks to its innovative products and wide-ranging services tailored to the customer's needs.

Within our International Implementation team we accompany our international customers from the signature of their contract to the hand over to our services teams. In this way we guarantee smooth and clear... integration of the agreed contractual deliverables so that as a result we have satisfied customers and happy SD Worx employees.

What do we have to offer?
• An attractive salary based on your experience and achievement. And the freedom to compose your personal benefit package.
• A dynamic environment: flexible working hours and working from home – everything is negotiable
• Learning opportunities: through an individual development plan and professional training
• Career growth: whether you want to become more of an expert in your field our you want to expand your knowledge more horizontally, there is always room to grow within SD Worx!

What do you have to offer?
• You have a Master's degree or equivalent through experience;
• You have at least 8 years of experience in project/ program management;
• You have experience in the roll-out of various international projects;
• You have experience with change management;
• You have experience with project methodology for implementation processes in HR and Payroll. Experience with Workday, SuccessFactors, Dayforce is an advantage;
• You have strong leadership abilities and people skills;
• You are a forceful communicator and have the necessary persuasiveness;
• You are professional, organized and results-oriented;
• You are commercially-minded and customer-friendly;
• You are fluent in English. Any other language is an advantage;
• You are flexible, also with regard to travelling internationally occasionally.

Which tasks can you expect?
• Managing various and complex projects in a multi-vendor environment where you ensure good monitoring of scope, budget and timing;
• Maintaining active and open communication with all internal and external stakeholders;
• Keeping multiple project teams on track;
• Create a positive and collaborative environment with quality and client experience as key points;
• Guiding and supporting pre-sales processes where you as the project manager - internal and external - speak to the customer in a pragmatic and professional way;
• Reporting to the client and internally;
• Setting up international project governance and steering;
• Flexible approach in potential changes in projects and steering on mitigation actions
• Assessment of project changes impact (scope, time, resources, pricing) and proposing and managing corrective actions
• Monitoring your project costs and revenue
• Monitoring and contribute to improvements in the existing implementation processes;
• Cooperation with and transfer to service delivery and key account managers;
• Expressing as ambassador the project methodology within and outside SD Worx.

From many places, we work as one, moving from better to best together.

SD Worx lives diversity in the workplace. Diversity provides inspiration and innovation in our company. We particularly welcome applications from qualified talent, regardless of origin, nationality, gender, skin colour, ethnic and social background, religion, age, disability, sexual orientation and stage of life

